WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.931 --> 00:00:03.197
- [Narrator] This is Pierce,

00:00:03.197 --> 00:00:05.594
an African crested porcupine.

00:00:05.594 --> 00:00:08.837
(piano music)

00:00:08.837 --> 00:00:11.048
The largest porcupine in the world,

00:00:11.048 --> 00:00:14.068
it can weigh over 60 pounds.

00:00:14.068 --> 00:00:16.022
When alarmed, its coarse quills

00:00:16.022 --> 00:00:19.274
can be raised into a
crest, making themselves

00:00:19.274 --> 00:00:22.355
look a lot bigger than they are.

00:00:22.355 --> 00:00:25.591
It is mostly heavily
armored in its hind quarters

00:00:25.591 --> 00:00:28.147
which have short, thick quills.

00:00:28.147 --> 00:00:31.629
These quills can get stuck
into its predator's skin.

00:00:31.629 --> 00:00:34.513
A good weapon when dealing
with hyenas, leopards

00:00:34.513 --> 00:00:35.763
and even lions.

00:00:36.976 --> 00:00:38.836
Pierce is mostly a herbivore,

00:00:38.836 --> 00:00:41.682
eating roots, bulbs and crops,

00:00:41.682 --> 00:00:44.315
along with the occasional insect.

00:00:44.315 --> 00:00:46.368
Unfortunately for his species,

00:00:46.368 --> 00:00:49.895
crested porcupines are seen
as an agricultural pest

00:00:49.895 --> 00:00:52.966
and as open land rapidly shrinks,

00:00:52.966 --> 00:00:55.502
they come into closer
quarters with farmers

00:00:55.502 --> 00:00:58.732
who will hunt them out of their home.

00:00:58.732 --> 00:01:01.899
This is the African crested porcupine.

